er resolves the login location if it is queue-tagged, otherwise its nearest queue-tagged ancestor, and stores that as `selectedQueueLocationUuid` (`queue-location-header-title.component.tsx:35-41`, persisted at `:50-58`).\n- Before the fix, the form's default was only `sessionLocation?.uuid`. For a non-queue-tagged login location, no option matched, so the select rendered blank.\n- After the fix, the default is `selectedQueueLocationUuid ?? sessionLocation?.uuid ?? ''`, so the form picks up the ancestor the dashboard chose.\n\n**Caveat:** The fix only reads the stored value. If the form is opened without the header having run in this session, the store can be empty and the field still falls back to the session location, which may be blank. The PR review (dkayiwa) raised the ancestor case and the effect-based version; the final version drops the effect and reads the store at mount.\n\n**Evidence, best first**\n\n1. `openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/create-queue-entry/queue-fields/queue-fields.component.tsx:81`: the changed default value (the actual fix).\n2. `openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/create-queue-entry/queue-fields/queue-fields.component.tsx:68`: `selectedQueueLocationUuid` read from the store.\n3. `openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/patient-queue-header/queue-location-header-title.component.tsx:35-41`: nearest queue-tagged ancestor resolution.\n4. `openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/patient-queue-header/queue-location-header-title.component.tsx:50-58`: the resolved location is written to the store.\n5. `openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/store/store.ts:45-48`: `updateSelectedQueueLocationUuid` and its store update.\n6. `openmrs-esm-patient-management/packages/esm-service-queues-app/src/create-queue-entry/queue-fields/queue-fields.test.tsx:225-240`: new tests for prefill from the store and the sess